Usage: /home/xinra/qcp-binary-democases/linux-binary/symexec [options] [input-file]

Run symbolic execution and generate verification conditions.

General:
  -h, --help                     Show this help message
  @<file>                        Read additional command line arguments from file
  --args-file <file>             Read additional command line arguments from file

Input:
  --input-file <file>            Read program input from a file
  <input-file>                   Read program input from a file
  --compile-commands <file>      Read include paths from compile_commands.json
  -I<path>                       Add a header search path
  --input-file-name <name>       Override the displayed input file name

Output:
  --gen-and-backup               Backup generated files before overwriting
  --coq-output-dir <dir>         Derive generated Coq file paths from an output folder
  --lean-output-dir <dir>        Enable Lean generation and derive generated Lean file paths from an output folder
  --goal-file <file>             Write generated proof goals to a file
  --proof-auto-file <file>       Write the auto proof script to a file
  --proof-manual-file <file>     Write the manual proof script to a file
  --no-coq-gen                   Disable all Coq file generation
  --no-lean-gen                  Disable all Lean file generation
  --program-path <file>          Write the generated Coq program to a file
  --Json-output                  Enable JSON output
  --soundness-proof              Generate soundness proof artifacts

Logic:
  -slp <folder> <logic-path>     Map a strategy folder to a Coq logic path
  --coq-logic-path <path>        Set the Coq logical path for generated files
  --lean-logic-path <path>       Set the Lean import prefix for generated files
  --CRules <module>              Import the given CRules module
  --arch <32|64>                 Select target C architecture width (default: 32)
  --endian <big|little>          Select target byte order (default: big)
  --no-CRules                    Do not import the default CRules module
  --no-logic-path                Do not assign a Coq logical path

Strategy:
  --strategy-file <file>         Load strategy configuration from a file
  --no-strategy-gen              Skip strategy soundness goal generation
  --strategy-application-limit <count> Stop a solver run after this many successful strategy applications (default: 4096)
  --no-record-strategies         Disable builtin record strategies
  --strategy-application-limit <count> Stop a solver run after this many successful strategy applications (default: 4096)
  --no-record-strategies         Disable builtin record strategies
  --export-record-strategy-dir <dir> Export generated record strategies to a directory

Execution:
  -s <mode>                      Select execution mode: 0=normal symbolic execution, 1=print parser partial-program output and stop after type checking, 2=print elaborated partial statements, 3=print the completed PSTree, 4=legacy StateMachineTest-compatible normal execution, 5=legacy reserved normal execution
  --conassertion                 Use conassertion mode
  --debug-preprocessor           Print macro expansions during preprocessing
  --no-exec-info                 Suppress execution progress output
  --full-auto                    Enable fully automatic proof mode
  --float-finite-vc              Generate finite safety VCs for floating-point operations
  --no-float-finite-vc           Do not generate finite safety VCs for floating-point operations

Diagnostics:
  --dump-smt-vc-file <file>      Dump generated SMT verification conditions
  --Auto-VC-Checking <file>      Print strategies' Exists instantiations and intermediate props during VC proving
  --disable-solver-info          Suppress solver-related output

Assertion format:
  --basic-assertion              Use the basic separation logic assertion format
  --primary-assertion            Use the primary assertion format
  --inner-assertion              Use the PROP LOCAL SEP assertion format
  --user-assertion               Use the user-facing assertion format

